LayerBench

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers LayerBench's own work. It does not cover the material below,
which the repository cites or keeps and credits to its source, and LayerBench does not relicense
it:

- The definitions and band thresholds cited from the Keyboard Layouts Doc (3rd edition).
- From cyanophage's Keyboard Layout Playground (https://cyanophage.github.io/playground.html):
  its per-key Effort costs and their scale of 577, the colour ramp of its per-finger SFB bars, and
  the numbers it printed for ten layouts, pinned with the layout strings its index uses in
  apps/web/e2e/cyanophage/. The playground's repository declares no licence.
- The bundled layouts other authors designed, each credited in its definition to its author, and
  to its source where the definition links one (packages/core/src/layouts, and their copies in
  packages/core/golden/layouts). Among them is cyanophage's Sunlight
  (https://cyanophage.github.io/#sunlight), kept in the playground's repository, which declares no
  licence.
- The corpus texts in packages/corpora/raw and the samples built from them in
  apps/web/public/corpora, each under the licence recorded with its source in
  packages/corpora/raw/sources.json.

What LayerBench takes from each source, and what is its own, is in docs/METRICS.md, under
"Implementation and attribution".
